id: pm-e97jyf
title: "Linked-test schema context changes non-PM repository checks, so commands that pass directly fail when recorded and run through pm test"
description: "The 2026-08-04 audit linked existing sandbox-safe repository commands to its PM plan. The focused merge suite passed directly at 120/120, but pm test default schema context failed 1/120 because validate_merge_driver_configuration warnings appeared only under the linked sandbox. The 10k scale gate passed directly, but failed under the same inherited PM_PATH context with token and latency threshold changes. Build/typecheck and published-release verification passed in both contexts. The runner correctly isolates tracker mutations, but it silently changes semantics for non-PM commands that already create their own fixtures."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:tests",environment-parity,linked-tests,regression
created_at: "2026-08-04T09:30:07.005Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-22T07:38:04.814Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Per-test execution context is explicit, persisted, and visible before command execution.; Self-sandboxing repository test and benchmark commands have parity between direct and linked execution without access to real tracker data.; Merge and scale regression fixtures cover schema, tracker-copy, and self-sandboxing modes with guided recovery.; The runner distinguishes assertion failure caused by execution context from an actual product gate regression."
why_now: "The 2026-08-22 ecosystem review reproduced the same trust failure on current binaries: a real-tracker changelog check passed unchanged, while the identical linked command failed because PM_PATH selected a tracker snapshot but the workspace-relative CHANGELOG.md still pointed at the source checkout. The runner needs an explicit paired tracker-and-workspace snapshot contract for repository checks."
parent: pm-92if
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "pm CLI 2026.8.4, linked-test default pm_context_mode=schema"
repro_steps: "Link the focused merge suite and pnpm benchmark:scale:check to a PM item, run pm test <id> --run --progress, then run the same commands directly through scripts/run-tests.mjs and pnpm."
expected_result: "Sandbox-safe commands produce the same assertions and performance contract directly and through pm test, with explicit context metadata where semantic differences are intentional."
actual_result: Direct merge tests pass 120/120 and direct scale gate passes; linked schema context produces merge-driver configuration warnings and scale token/latency threshold failures.
customer_impact: Agents cannot trust the canonical linked-test evidence loop and may misclassify orchestration-context failures as product regressions.
