comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T09:30:24.732Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-04: searched all statuses for linked-test schema sandbox, PM_PATH merge-driver warnings, non-PM benchmark context drift, direct-versus-linked parity, and self-sandboxing repository commands. Closed pm-uawujr fixed package prepare source fallback; closed pm-oslr delivered linked execution; open pm-ed28wi owns trust/allowlisting. None owns the reproduced semantic parity failure for already-sandboxed non-PM commands."
  "2026-08-22T07:27:50.502Z","harness:codex","Recurrence evidence (2026-08-22): pnpm changelog:pm:check passed directly against the live project and reported CHANGELOG.md unchanged with 2,167 closed items. When linked with pm_context_mode=tracker, pm test copied all 2,534 tracker items into the sandbox but retained the source checkout as the output-file workspace; the extension generated from the sandbox tracker and compared against CHANGELOG.md, then falsely reported it out of date. This is the existing issue, so no duplicate was created. The tracker-quality assurance command did pass in tracker context, proving that per-test context metadata works when the command has no coupled source-workspace artifact."
  "2026-08-22T07:37:11.696Z","harness:codex","Hosted recurrence evidence (2026-08-22): the exact-head static gate correctly rejected a host-specific absolute checkout path in this item. pm history-redact preview found one historical and one projected-item occurrence with zero preexisting hash mismatch; the applied redaction replaced it with workspace-relative CHANGELOG.md, recomputed the chain, appended an audited history_redact marker, and verified the resulting stream."
body: "Design a deterministic execution-context contract for linked tests. Detect commands that use scripts/run-tests.mjs or self-contained benchmark fixtures; do not inject an empty schema PM_PATH when it changes their meaning, or require and persist an explicit per-test context mode with a clear add-time diagnostic. The output must show the effective context before execution and recommend the correct bounded retry. Preserve the rule that tests never read or write real repository PM data."
